<div id="2026-09-10-traveler-section-cards" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-10 — Traveler parts view grouped into normally-closed section cards</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Replaced the single flat table in the traveler view with five normally-closed collapsible cards, each grouping parts by their current workflow stage: Items to Order (amber), Need to Add to Print Queue (purple), In Print Queue (red), Printed/Arrived — Ready to Pick (blue), and Picked — In Pick Box (green). Each card shows its part count, a colored header matching the existing traveler color scheme, and a click-to-open table. Cards start closed. The "Items to Order" card includes a direct Order link to each part's <code>/Inventory/item/view</code> page. Each part row now also includes inline STL upload (download + upload label beside it) matching the print queue style.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The user wanted the traveler to sort items into logical workflow sections so staff can focus on one stage at a time: what needs ordering → what needs queueing → what's printing → what's ready to pick → what's in the box.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>root/Accounting/Manufacturing/traveler_view.tt</code> (complete rewrite of the body section — 5 collapsible cards, grouping by row_state, STL upload in action column, Order link for bought items).</p>
</div>